# fp8 SDPA shapes.
# Format: Q_dims:K_dims:V_dims  (batch x heads x seq x head_dim)
#   Q = mb x H_q  x S_q  x d_qk
#   K = mb x H_kv x d_qk x S_kv   (K stored transposed)
#   V = mb x H_kv x S_kv x d_v
#
# head_size selects the Q staging path on targets with a native fp8 systolic
# multiply:
#   d_qk >= 64  -> Q stays fp8 through SLM, packed 4 elements per 32-bit word
#   d_qk <= 32  -> falls back to the f16 upconvert, because the packed Q tile
#                  would be narrower than a subgroup
# Both are covered deliberately so the fallback does not go untested.

# --- d_qk = 64: native fp8 Q staging
1x16x384x64:1x16x64x384:1x16x384x64
2x8x384x64:2x8x64x384:2x8x384x64

# --- d_qk = 128: native fp8 Q staging, larger tile
1x32x512x128:1x32x128x512:1x32x512x128

# --- d_qk = 32: forces the f16 upconvert path even where fp8 is native
1x8x256x32:1x8x32x256:1x8x256x32

# --- GQA, LLaMA-3-8B style: q_heads=32, kv_heads=8
1x32x384x128:1x8x128x384:1x8x384x128

# --- GQA, Qwen2-7B style: q_heads=28, kv_heads=4
1x28x384x128:1x4x128x384:1x4x384x128

# --- S_kv not a multiple of the workgroup tile: exercises the remainder path
1x16x129x64:1x16x64x129:1x16x129x64

# --- Thin Q (decode-style single query against a long KV cache)
1x32x1x128:1x32x128x512:1x32x512x128
